{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3064","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3064","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3064\",\"parent_revision\":\"e4efd4d1705583aa4af20ed28d364f7b147ace690f3b8b19ce65f2b32713b198\",\"root_revision\":\"e4efd4d1705583aa4af20ed28d364f7b147ace690f3b8b19ce65f2b32713b198\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSeveral grooming agents are instructed to fetch the full item explicitly. Under R3 the compact form is automatic when content exceeds budget, so these instructions ask for behaviour the contract supersedes and defeat the sizing they exist within.\\n\\nOne agent already scopes its read to named sections; the others do not.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] No agent instruction directs fetching a full item as its default read\\n- [ ] Agent instructions describe requesting the parts needed, by address or name\\n- [ ] Instructions do not restate the contract; they point to it\\n- [ ] Agents that must read several sections request them in one scoped call\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P2 \u2014 corrects instructions; behaviour also improves once hint strings are fixed\\n- Related: #2453 (agents hardcode section names with no route to a source of truth)\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e05b6e7f13388e3e8722112452dbb830e6a75880e34ca5dec7b60cdb45e1689a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvdiDQ\"}"}